    "title": "Wojo: Tigers enjoy a perfect opening in Detroit with new talent, energy",
    "text": "BOB WOJNOWSKIWojo: Tigers enjoy Opening Day blast, with another McGonigle boost Bob WojnowskiThe Detroit NewsApril 3, 2026Updated April 4, 2026, 4:45 a.m. ETSubscribe to hear this storyDetroit — Most of the same players, all of the same goals. But a new home season for the Tigers also meant invigorating new sights and scenes, including something we hadn’t felt in 35 years — 70-degree weather on Opening Day.The warmth spread through Comerica Park, and not just because the sunny breeze was spectacular. There was a new strong-armed pitcher with All-Star credentials in Framber Valdez on the mound. There was a renewed strong-armed pitcher in Justin Verlander, back after a nine-year absence, preparing for his Sunday home debut as the oldest player in the majors at 43.",
